Why Argo CD? Why not only CI tools like Jenkins or GitLab CI?
This is one of the most common Interview questions I see in DevOps interviews and real projects.
👉 “If we already have Jenkins or GitLab CI, why do we need Argo CD?”
Here’s the simple, real-world explanation 👇
🔹 What CI tools are best at
CI tools like Jenkins, GitLab CI, GitHub Actions are excellent for:
✅ Building applications
 ✅ Running tests
 ✅ Creating Docker images
 ✅ Pushing images to registries (ECR / Docker Hub)
 ✅ Updating Kubernetes manifests in Git
👉 CI = Build & Test
🔹 The limitation of CI-only deployments
When CI tools deploy directly to Kubernetes:
❌ Cluster credentials must be shared
 ❌ Deployments become push-based
 ❌ Rollbacks are manual
 ❌ Hard to track configuration changes
 ❌ Risk of configuration drift
This is where Argo CD becomes critical 👇
🔹 What exactly is Argo CD?
Argo CD is a GitOps-based Continuous Delivery (CD) tool for Kubernetes.
🔹 Git is the single source of truth
 🔹 Argo CD continuously watches Git
 🔹 It ensures actual cluster state = desired Git state
👉 Argo CD = Deploy & Maintain
🔹 How CI + Argo CD work together (Production Flow)
1️⃣ Developer pushes code to Git
 2️⃣ CI pipeline:
Builds the application
Runs tests
Builds Docker image
Pushes image to registry
Updates Kubernetes YAML in Git
3️⃣ Argo CD detects Git changes
 4️⃣ Argo CD syncs changes to Kubernetes
 5️⃣ If someone modifies the cluster manually → Argo CD detects drift and fixes it
✅ Secure
 ✅ Auditable
 ✅ Automated
 ✅ Production-ready
🔹 Why teams prefer Argo CD
✔ Pull-based (more secure)
 ✔ Automatic drift detection
 ✔ Easy rollback (just revert Git commit)
 ✔ Clear UI visibility
 ✔ Kubernetes-native CD
 ✔ Perfect for multi-env (dev / stage / prod)
🎯 Interview-Winning One-Liner
“CI tools build and test applications, while Argo CD deploys and continuously maintains Kubernetes workloads using GitOps.”
🔥 This single line creates impact.
💡 Final Thought
CI tools and Argo CD are not alternatives — they complement each other.
👉 CI builds the software
 👉 Argo CD runs and maintains it
